WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.568
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The Personal Bubble.

00:00:14.568 --> 00:00:21.136
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:21.136 --> 00:00:25.077
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:25.077 --> 00:00:29.018
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:29.018 --> 00:00:38.214
Around every body, there is an invisible bubble. You cannot see it, but you can feel where it is. It is the space that lets your body feel easy.

00:00:38.214 --> 00:00:48.723
Bubbles come in different sizes. Some people like hugs up close. Some people like an arm's length of room. Both sizes are fine. Neither one is wrong.

00:00:48.723 --> 00:01:00.546
Your bubble belongs to you. It goes where you go. And every person you meet is carrying one of their own.

00:01:00.546 --> 00:01:05.800
Bubbles work by asking. Let me show you how.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:17.623
Before a hug, before a tickle, before a hand on a shoulder — ask. Can I have a hug? May I sit close? Short question. Then wait.

00:01:17.623 --> 00:01:29.446
The answer rules. A yes means yes. And anything that is not a clear yes means stop.

00:01:29.446 --> 00:01:41.269
A no means stop. A step back means stop. A body that goes still and frozen means stop. Instantly, every time — no convincing, no teasing, no asking again.

00:01:41.269 --> 00:01:51.778
Stopping fast is not rude. Stopping fast is how bubbles stay safe. The person who stops when asked is the person everyone can trust.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.091
And the same rule protects you. Friends ask you. Grown-ups ask you. You may always say no to a hug — even a kind one, even from someone you love.

00:01:53.091 --> 00:02:04.914
There is one thing that is different from a hug, and it is important to know it. Keeping a body safe.

00:02:04.914 --> 00:02:16.737
A grown-up might hold your hand to cross the street, or catch you so you do not fall. That is safety help. It is not a hug, and it does not need the same ask.

00:02:16.737 --> 00:02:25.932
Everything else follows the bubble rule. Your bubble is never the wrong size. Nobody gets to laugh at it, shrink it, or talk you out of it.

00:02:25.932 --> 00:02:27.246
And today, nobody touches anybody. This whole practice happens in words and in imagination. Your bubble stays exactly where it is.

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:36.442
My bubble is mine. Your bubble is yours. The answer rules.

00:02:36.442 --> 00:02:43.010
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:48.264
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:48.264 --> 00:02:54.833
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:54.833 --> 00:03:01.401
You're ready for what's next.
